WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.890
People are definitely gonna be shocked.

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:12.643
We kept this a secret for like 40 weeks.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.850
Me being injured was like
a blessing in disguise.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:20.060
Those moments and memories were huge

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:23.200
for kind of what helped
blossom our relationship

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:24.533
into what it is.

00:00:28.452 --> 00:00:29.535
Are you...?

00:00:33.004 --> 00:00:35.740
I hope this continues to kinda show people

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:38.460
that there's no perfect way to find love,

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.603
or have a family or create a family.

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:47.855
We're just looking forward
to kind of continuing

00:00:47.855 --> 00:00:52.138
to write our story, but with...

00:00:52.138 --> 00:00:53.839
...with a baby.

00:00:53.839 --> 00:00:55.155
A little one.
Yeah.

00:01:01.263 --> 00:01:02.096
Oh my god.

00:01:03.153 --> 00:01:04.989
Are you nervous?

00:01:04.989 --> 00:01:05.822
Yeah!

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:08.808
You better talk more than me.

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:14.628
Why can't I be the best
player and also have a baby?

00:01:14.628 --> 00:01:15.628
But not carry a baby.

00:01:17.273 --> 00:01:18.823
You know, why can't we do both?

00:01:20.536 --> 00:01:24.795
WNBA Champion, Breanna Stewart.

00:01:24.795 --> 00:01:26.874
Stewart gets 15 seconds on the clock.

00:01:26.874 --> 00:01:29.040
Ball behind the back,
she'll lay it up and in.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:30.530
Really, are you gonna try

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:33.483
to put a hook shot up on Breanna Stewart?

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:37.233
Just a quick story.

00:01:37.233 --> 00:01:41.433
The night she got hurt,
that's the night we started.

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:46.750
I just remember being in such a place

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:51.171
where it was like, you know,
something terrible happened,

00:01:51.171 --> 00:01:52.990
and then at the same time
something amazing happened,

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:56.080
and I was like, is it any
way I can go back to Russia

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:57.280
with a torn achilles?

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:00.030
Can I just go there, and then go?

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:08.340
I had this ring made since November.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:10.940
And it was just about like
finding the right moment.

00:02:14.111 --> 00:02:16.835
What's up, guys? This is Devin, Katie Lou.

00:02:16.835 --> 00:02:20.204
We're here to witness the
greatest wedding of all time.

00:02:20.204 --> 00:02:21.096
Follow us.

00:02:22.153 --> 00:02:24.240
When I was younger did I have any idea

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.930
that I was going to marry a woman?

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:28.180
I had no idea,

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:30.010
but she's the one I want to be with,

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:32.801
and we are living our best life.

00:02:32.801 --> 00:02:33.760
From this day forward,

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:36.530
I promise to be your wife, and partner.

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:37.720
From this day forward,

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:40.207
I promise to be your wife, and partner.

00:02:41.157 --> 00:02:43.426
Marta, you may now kiss.

00:02:50.038 --> 00:02:51.104
You're married!

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:51.971
Yay!

00:02:57.948 --> 00:02:58.781
Cheers!

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:06.580
So, when I decided to freeze my eggs,

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:08.480
I really didn't know why I was doing it.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:09.627
If I'm gonna be honest,

00:03:09.627 --> 00:03:11.610
it was just the fact that I'm injured,

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:12.770
I can't play,

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:15.200
this is the perfect
opportunity, because when else

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:18.100
am I going to get a two-week
period where I'm not playing?

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:21.720
It was probably one of the
best decisions I've made,

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:22.860
really in my life,

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:25.360
because you're setting
yourself up for the future.

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:30.340
I've always felt that I
wanted to start a family

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:33.570
when I was younger, but as
a womens basketball player,

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:34.990
it's like, okay, how do you do that?

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:36.520
How do you plan that perfectly

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:39.170
so the baby comes in the summer?

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:43.230
Now, after the Olympics for 2021,

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:46.160
which well, we're cutting
it a little close.

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:46.993
Amor

00:03:48.178 --> 00:03:49.011
Where are we?

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:50.960
Idaho.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:52.990
What are we doing here?

00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:54.773
3D appointment for Ruby.

00:03:55.740 --> 00:03:56.833
So exciting!

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.881
Her lips.
I know.

00:03:59.881 --> 00:04:01.830
I'm like, whoa.

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:03.453
She has botox in there?!

00:04:06.271 --> 00:04:07.649
Wow, look at that.

00:04:07.649 --> 00:04:09.087
She has such round cheeks.

00:04:09.087 --> 00:04:10.970
Now it's 29 weeks.

00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:14.641
She looks like a 31 week baby.

00:04:14.641 --> 00:04:15.474
Yeah.

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:19.703
Four pounds.
This is her face.

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:22.718
Look at her lips.

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:25.910
Four pounds.
Four pounds,

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:27.800
two weeks ahead of schedule.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:30.775
We need her to stay in there-
Yes, please.

00:04:30.775 --> 00:04:33.353
'til her due date, 'cause of the Olympics.

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:39.348
And now we're going back to Seattle

00:04:39.348 --> 00:04:40.181
quick trip.

00:04:43.654 --> 00:04:47.150
Today we are going to put
together the stroller,

00:04:47.150 --> 00:04:48.930
because Ruby comes in eight weeks

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:52.938
and we need to get it together.

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:56.543
Oh, right here.

00:04:57.585 --> 00:04:58.418
Hah!

00:05:02.258 --> 00:05:03.183
Come here.

00:05:03.183 --> 00:05:04.440
Stew, you don't know what's happening.

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:06.427
Come here, we gotta test it out!

00:05:09.659 --> 00:05:11.011
How do we open this thing?

00:05:11.011 --> 00:05:13.747
Amor, we cannot teach him this already.

00:05:13.747 --> 00:05:14.580
Sit.

00:05:15.691 --> 00:05:16.524
Good boy.

00:05:17.607 --> 00:05:19.950
Shout out to Sami, Kate and Nash.

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:23.260
They sent us a little
care package of things

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:26.050
that they didn't know that they needed

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:27.770
when Nash was born.

00:05:27.770 --> 00:05:29.150
There's a hairbrush.

00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:31.265
That she said she's
gonna use it for herself.

00:05:31.265 --> 00:05:34.220
Yeah, maybe I'm gonna use it, too.

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:35.663
But I don't brush my hair.

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:38.850
I thought that was for Stew.

00:05:39.736 --> 00:05:41.032
What is it?

00:05:41.032 --> 00:05:42.433
It's a diaper bag.

00:05:42.433 --> 00:05:44.070
Oh.

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:45.736
Probably could use it for Stew, too.

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:49.610
Sorry.

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:50.553
The white noise.

00:05:53.123 --> 00:05:54.620
For the shh.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.096
I'm going to shush you.

00:05:57.521 --> 00:06:00.740
That's on our baby list.

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:03.010
Oh, and this is the thing
that I said I wanted,

00:06:03.010 --> 00:06:04.113
and Marta said,

00:06:04.113 --> 00:06:06.070
"I don't know if it's
comfortable for babies."

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:09.480
Nash would only go to sleep
in this when he was a baby.

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:12.560
This was a lifesaver, so
we didn't have to swaddle,

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:15.303
where the babies are
just stuck in that thing.

00:06:17.222 --> 00:06:19.183
And we just moved into our condo.

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:21.640
It's messy.

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:22.950
Un poco messy.

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:24.433
But look at the kitchen.

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:27.043
In that one.

00:06:27.043 --> 00:06:28.653
She has a fire diaper bag.

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:31.333
This one?

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:36.010
Look at it.

00:06:36.010 --> 00:06:37.370
We just needed it.

00:06:39.270 --> 00:06:40.840
You know, obviously, I'm not pregnant.

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:42.110
They're like, is Marta pregnant?

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:44.763
Marta can't be 34 weeks
pregnant right now.

00:06:47.270 --> 00:06:49.570
So just explaining the whole situation,

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:51.933
about how it's a little different,

00:06:51.933 --> 00:06:54.262
how we started it,

00:06:54.262 --> 00:06:58.940
how, like using a surrogate.

00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:00.870
But I think that's one of the experiences

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:03.630
that makes it kind of cool

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:06.350
for people to see like other sides

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:10.553
of more than just
traditionally having a baby.

00:07:12.010 --> 00:07:14.906
She wanted to get this
just in case we go to Cabo.

00:07:14.906 --> 00:07:16.547
Oh yeah, we're going to Cabo.

00:07:18.139 --> 00:07:19.880
We are going on a vacation.

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:21.050
I don't know where we're going,

00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:22.475
but we are going somewhere.

00:07:23.730 --> 00:07:27.546
Ruby is thirty...

00:07:27.546 --> 00:07:28.697
four weeks.

00:07:28.697 --> 00:07:31.090
34 weeks.
34 weeks.

00:07:31.090 --> 00:07:33.180
The size of a pineapple.

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:35.350
I guess a big pineapple.

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:38.160
She's five pounds, right now,

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:39.423
with six weeks to go.

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:43.891
So, this is how it looks right now.

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:53.173
Tomorrow they're bringing
the bed and the chair.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:08:00.200
We are missing the shelves,
but Stew is being nosy already.

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:03.450
Well, she's going to be an amazing mom.

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:06.170
We've got two amazing moms
we're going to have here.

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:07.130
So this is...

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:12.220
It's-
Hold it together.

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:13.285
I know.

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:17.070
Even like with her,
with her dog, you know,

00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:19.270
so she's very protective of the dog.

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:22.973
She's gonna be a pretty
emotional mom, I think.

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:27.060
What I realized was, what
do you want for your kids?

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:29.703
You know, you want them
to be happy, that's it.

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:33.120
You just want them to be happy.

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:33.993
And she's happy.

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:38.330
And my mom says all the time, like,

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:41.993
I've never seen you so
happy, and feeling so free.

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:45.640
Even the last time we
were together at home,

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:48.847
she was like, "You're more
nicer when she's around."

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:53.180
She said, and her mom sends

00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:56.460
random voice notes on WhatsApp,

00:08:56.460 --> 00:08:58.560
like just crying, she's crying,

00:08:58.560 --> 00:08:59.590
and I don't know what she's saying,

00:08:59.590 --> 00:09:00.947
but I'm like, "what is she saying?"

00:09:00.947 --> 00:09:04.297
and she's like, "She's just
so happy that we're happy."

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:08.280
How, when, if, are you
gonna tell your child

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:15.860
about how she was brought into this world?

00:09:16.170 --> 00:09:18.520
And I think for us is

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:21.660
we're just gonna continue to be honest,

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:24.030
be genuine, be authentic.

00:09:24.030 --> 00:09:26.620
I think the same way that we are

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:28.920
in our lives, with the rest of the world,

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:32.160
like that's how we're gonna be with Ruby.

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:34.193
She deserves to know the entire process.

00:09:40.280 --> 00:09:41.350
I think we're ready.

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:43.450
Yeah.
And if not, we go shopping.

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:44.870
I can't believe this
is actually happening.

00:09:44.870 --> 00:09:46.050
I'm still in shock.

00:09:46.050 --> 00:09:47.143
I'm still in shock.

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:53.330
This is our last night
together before I go to Tokyo.

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:57.560
We have only 28 days left until she comes.

00:09:57.560 --> 00:10:00.580
We have 45 minutes left together,

00:10:00.580 --> 00:10:03.577
because she has another thing to do.

00:10:03.577 --> 00:10:08.577
And also being the two of us
until the little one comes.

00:10:09.095 --> 00:10:10.322
Yep.

00:10:10.322 --> 00:10:11.950
It's about to be three.

00:10:11.950 --> 00:10:13.193
With a gold medal.

00:10:15.599 --> 00:10:16.432
Yes.

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:24.840
Being in Tokyo with the gold medal

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:26.250
being put around my neck,

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:28.150
it's just even more worth it.

00:10:28.150 --> 00:10:30.700
I've always been on big stages,

00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:34.360
but now it's more than
me, and more than us.

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:37.660
But for this little one to kinda

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:39.901
see what she can do.

00:10:44.587 --> 00:10:47.490
I can't believe it's actually,
the day is actually here.

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:50.243
It's happening.

00:10:50.243 --> 00:10:52.193
I just got back from Tokyo yesterday,

00:10:53.230 --> 00:10:55.613
landed in LA, flew to Idaho,

00:10:56.707 --> 00:10:58.882
and now we're here.

00:10:59.892 --> 00:11:00.811
What is jet lag?

00:11:00.811 --> 00:11:03.503
What even is jet lag?
I don't know.

00:12:10.386 --> 00:12:13.370
I had this idea where I was like,

00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:16.037
her middle name should be Tokyo.

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:24.860
First of all, we don't
have middle names in Spain,

00:12:24.860 --> 00:12:27.347
so it's like, that's another
thing that I was like,

00:12:27.347 --> 00:12:29.590
"Okay, just something easy.

00:12:29.590 --> 00:12:31.750
I'm not going to call her Ruby Tokyo."

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:34.800
That, I'm like, "That
doesn't go together."

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:36.470
And then with all these surnames,

00:12:36.470 --> 00:12:39.240
because we need to figure
out about the surnames.

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:42.127
It's like, okay, just choose another one.

00:12:43.970 --> 00:12:46.050
So now the next dog will be Tokyo.

00:12:46.050 --> 00:12:47.950
Because she wants a puppy, you know?

00:12:49.320 --> 00:12:50.809
Stew needs a friend.

00:12:50.809 --> 00:12:52.493
He's gonna have Ruby.

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:55.140
So-
I'm like,

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:56.930
I don't know whose life
is going to change more

00:12:56.930 --> 00:12:58.063
his or ours.

